# CLAUDE.md

{{PROJECT_NAME}} — Next.js {{NEXT_VERSION}} + Payload CMS v3 + PostgreSQL. One application: frontend, admin panel, API, and all backend logic live in this repo and deploy as one unit.

## Stack Rules

- **Backend logic runs on the stack itself**: user-triggered mutations are Server Actions (`src/actions/`), rules that must always hold are Payload hooks (`src/hooks/`), async/scheduled work is the Payload Jobs Queue (`src/jobs/`). No external workflow engine.
- **Enforce in hooks, pre-check in actions** — admin panel and REST bypass actions; hooks and access control are the authority.
- **Every user-facing Local API call** passes `overrideAccess: false, user` — the Local API skips access control by default.
- **Reads go through `src/lib/queries/`** helpers returning typed DTOs (`depth: 0` unless justified); pages never call `payload.find` inline.
- **Types are generated**: run `pnpm generate:types` after any schema change; import from `@/payload-types`.
- **Postgres schema**: dev uses push; production uses committed migrations (`pnpm payload migrate:create <name>` when a feature is done). Never mix push and migrate on one database.

## Layout

```
src/
├── payload.config.ts      # collections, globals, jobs, plugins — read this first
├── collections/           # CollectionConfig per file (+ colocated integration tests)
├── globals/               # settings singletons
├── access/roles.ts        # role helpers + Access functions (shared by UI and data layer)
├── hooks/                 # collection/field hooks (thin; pure helpers alongside)
├── jobs/                  # TaskConfig / WorkflowConfig
├── actions/               # 'use server' actions per domain
├── lib/session.ts         # getSession(): { payload, user }
├── lib/queries/           # read helpers → DTOs
├── seed/                  # seed scripts (pnpm seed)
└── app/
    ├── (frontend)/        # product UI (own root layout)
    └── (payload)/         # admin + REST/GraphQL (Payload-owned; do not add pages here)
```

## Commands

```bash
pnpm dev                   # Next dev + admin at /admin
pnpm generate:types        # payload-types.ts from payload.config.ts
pnpm payload migrate:create <name>
pnpm test                  # vitest (unit + integration)
pnpm seed                  # seed data
```

## Environment

Secrets in `.env` (never committed): `DATABASE_URI`, `PAYLOAD_SECRET`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL`, `ENABLE_JOBS`, `PAYLOAD_MCP_URL`, `PAYLOAD_MCP_API_KEY`. See `.env.example` for the full catalogue.

## Feature Workflow

Follow the nine-step recipe (collection → access → hooks → types → jobs → actions → queries → UI → tests + migration) from the `stack-nextjs-payloadcms-dev` plugin's `full-feature` skill.
